      "sha256": "dae161c9201d44023d689455e6f023a56cb6189d5cb305c7aa4a235b44e95741",
      "size_bytes": 9151,
      "full_source_read": true,
      "line_count": 221,
      "reviewed_lines": [
        [
          1,
          221
        ]
      ],
      "assessment": "Read all221 lines. Exact BigRational entries reject zero denominators and normalize before multiplication. General sensing admits compatible shapes without demanding invisible repairs; strengthening to a quotient report checks every entry of R*d0=0. For Q-vector spaces that condition exactly states constancy on cosets of im(d0). Blindspot records replay the actual supplied repair and report, distinguishing zero from nontrivial hidden repairs. Public DTO forgery is checked by full recomputation. Finite-dimensional rational carriers are not finite sets, as the source explicitly notes; no physical or semantic extraction follows. Three embedded tests cover meaningful visible/hidden/zero/forged/shape cases. Independent81-map-pair control checks2187 shifts; no original execution."
    },
    {
      "path": "code/rust/core_linear_algebra/src/proof.rs",
      "sha256": "b7e5a1c6f12255f95201c848b59e389f68950fed9ccb7a6cd49e9a2414f949f6",
      "size_bytes": 9899,
      "full_source_read": true,
      "line_count": 354,
      "reviewed_lines": [
        [
          1,
          354
        ]
      ],
      "assessment": "Read all354 lines. IDs reject blank text but retain untrimmed nonempty values; hash wrappers accept arbitrary32-byte caller input. TheoremProvenance is a public descriptive enum, including caller-selectable VerifiedByComputation and unchecked TheoremBoundary, without authentication or theorem checking. Symmetric/positive-definite witnesses have private fields and crate-private unchecked constructors whose checked path is explicitly not wired here; metadata tests inspect those fields, not the mathematical predicate. No public ingress bypass is inferred solely from crate-private constructors, and no original execution occurred."
    },
    {
      "path": "code/rust/core_linear_algebra/src/row_constraint_implication.rs",
      "sha256": "996e18fdcd0ef25eb453992904048d2155a11bb982f894d671ac5d1bb76e9a91",
      "size_bytes": 6201,
      "full_source_read": true,
      "line_count": 181,
      "reviewed_lines": [
        [
          1,
          181
        ]
      ],
      "assessment": "Read all181 lines. Classifier delegates solving D^T*c=row to exact-field elimination (owner now fully read and separately assessed), then separately replays either the complete row combination or a separating vector satisfying D*v=0 and row*v!=0. These are valid rational homogeneous-equation implication certificates for well-formed rationals. Public replay and denominator clearing do not themselves admit raw zero-denominator ratios; well-formed input is a necessary premise. Declared limits explicitly concern matrix allocation and solver operations, not scalar bit lengths, total heap or time. Denominator product is sufficient, not minimal. Sole inline mutation test checks literal Ok/Err and supplies no evidence for the implication owner; no native execution."
    },
    {
      "path": "code/rust/core_linear_algebra/src/scalars.rs",
      "sha256": "0f931d158060c86fba23d0077ab6265e3feafff609601b9ffc40c9bddb8bba2b",
      "size_bytes": 11298,
      "full_source_read": true,
      "line_count": 364,
      "reviewed_lines": [
        [
          1,
          364
        ],
        [
          1,
          115
        ],
        [
          145,
          180
        ]
      ],
      "assessment": "Read all 364 lines. Public Semiring/Ring/Field/ExactRing interfaces specify operations but cannot enforce algebraic laws of user implementations. A separate sealed CheckedExactField admits only Rational64/BigRational and uses fallible arithmetic, explicitly excluding truncating integer division and floats. BigRational has unbounded exact scalar operations under dependency correctness and available resources. i64 is tagged ExactRing with raw add/mul/neg; integer interpretation requires representability of every intermediate and cannot be inferred from that marker alone. Test-only Z5 requires residues0..4 although its tuple constructor does not normalize; its small arithmetic tests stay in range. Capacity record only checks1<=items<=capacity, unrelated to field laws. Numerical computational-profile and mutation-count comments supply no new execution evidence."
    },
    {
      "path": "code/rust/core_linear_algebra/src/semiring_lumpability.rs",
      "sha256": "8fcafc3a8d758182ffc345d94b23ccdc649aefe1948fe7fcf7a91662fe464a32",
      "size_bytes": 10713,
      "full_source_read": true,
      "line_count": 305,
      "reviewed_lines": [
        [
          1,
          305
        ]
      ],
      "assessment": "Read all305 lines. Generic ordered product uses only declared semiring operations. Membership validates exhaustive disjoint nonempty blocks, including the unique empty partition. Quotient reads one representative block sum and checks every other representative; MH=HB is exactly the length-one criterion, and associativity/distributivity inductively give M^nH=HB^n. This needs no subtraction or scalar multiplicative commutativity and preserves endpoint-block aggregates, not individual paths. Push-forward computes P*M*P^T for an admitted finite map, with loops/reverse arcs independent. Strong finite mathematical core with scalar-law and resource premises; substantive small tests plus unrelated capacity tests are retained. Independent162 small matrix/partition pairs give100 admissions checked through power5. No original execution."
    },
    {
      "path": "code/rust/core_linear_algebra/src/semiring_matrix.rs",
      "sha256": "0b42adc9683669747f463f7a9691f52808012bffee0099adca5d521ac9c5de3a",
      "size_bytes": 10616,
      "full_source_read": true,
      "line_count": 306,
      "reviewed_lines": [
        [
          1,
          306
        ]
      ],
      "assessment": "Read all306 lines. Shape-checked semiring multiplication, repeated-squaring powers and exhaustive Boolean square roots for n<=3 are substantive bounded algorithms. Boolean OR/AND operations are lawful; enumeration visits every2^(n*n) candidate and returns no partial answer on over-cap n. Independent relational composition checks all512 Boolean3x3 candidates. Named MAX_SCALAR_OPERATIONS counts dot-product terms although each term calls mul and add;256x256 multiplication passes with2^24 terms but2^25 scalar method calls. Each power multiplication gets a fresh per-call bound, not a total exponentiation budget. to_rows has no element/row-output quota; a zero-column source can still request many empty rows. Generic scalar law/representability premises persist. Real finite root/power tests and unrelated capacity tests were read, not executed."
    },
    {
      "path": "code/rust/core_linear_algebra/src/tensor/tensor_view.rs",
      "sha256": "255f901a159fc192f28e7c69b83475172607cf95f73adcaccb9c686d97bd7296",
